    "uid": "472008195ce14b51ddbe75664b13be38",
    "title": "Local account created",
    "desc": "A new local user account was created - useradd, adduser, newusers, or BSD pw useradd. A fresh account is a durable backdoor (a way back in, a second identity to pivot through), and it is a rare, deliberate administrative act, so on most hosts any creation is worth a look (MITRE T1136.001). An account created with uid/gid 0, or a home of /root, is escalation and worse. usermod/passwd on an existing account are left to the credential and privilege rules.",
